<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17195" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρεμ-ίζω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῐῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.68
				</span></i>
			.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β́</span>: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠτρέμισα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Morb.Sacr.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			:—<i>keep quiet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				303
			</span></i>: in 
				Ion.
			 Prose, mostly with neg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπίδος
				. . οὐδαμὰ ἀτρεμιζούσης</span> never <i>being kept
				still,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.74
			</span></i>; of restless, aggressive kings or nations, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀτρεμίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.185
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				190
			</span></i>; of people attacked, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτε αὐτοὺς οἰκὸς . . ἀτρεμιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.68
				</span></i>
			.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β́</span>; without a neg., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνώμην εἶχον ἀτρεμίζοντά σε
					μακαριστὸν εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.18
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.Sacr.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>.—Not in good 
				Att.
			, exc. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				2.4.9
			</span></i> (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεωτερίζειν</span>), cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				3.4.4
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>: also in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Ti.Locr.
				104b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				43.35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				26.317a
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
